WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:03.290
- So, you obviously know Jim and James.

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:06.072
- I know, I've met Jim once or twice.

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:07.640
We've hung out a couple times.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.550
You've come to a couple of shows.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.440
This is very exciting to be, you know--

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:11.273
- Oh, that's right.

00:00:11.273 --> 00:00:12.250
'Cause you're the animation,

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:13.083
so you didn't actually do a scene.

00:00:13.083 --> 00:00:14.067
You were in a booth.
- They put me in a booth.

00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:14.900
They put me in a booth.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:15.733
- [James] They do a movie--

00:00:15.733 --> 00:00:17.079
- [Jim] He makes sound--

00:00:17.079 --> 00:00:18.080
(laughing)

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:19.510
- [Ben] in front of nobody.
- You had the best job

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:21.120
because you could be in
pajamas doing your job.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:21.953
- Oh, yeah.

00:00:21.953 --> 00:00:23.450
I was literally like in
an old school nightie

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:25.024
with a candle and a hat.

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:26.050
(laughing)

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:27.110
Going around like Ebenezer Scrooge.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:28.548
- Why are you a Golden
Girl? Okay, I'm sorry.

00:00:28.548 --> 00:00:29.381
(laughing)

00:00:29.381 --> 00:00:30.214
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:30.214 --> 00:00:31.775
I dressed like all three
of the Golden Girls.

00:00:31.775 --> 00:00:32.608
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:00:32.608 --> 00:00:33.441
- Hot.

00:00:33.441 --> 00:00:34.482
I like it.
- Yeah, thanks!

00:00:34.482 --> 00:00:35.570
- So hot! Love it.

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:36.940
So, we also worked together

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:38.120
and we never met because we both--

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:39.450
- Yes, I was in a booth for that, too.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.260
- Yes, for Home. So I
did the voice thing, too.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:42.093
Yeah, we never met.

00:00:42.093 --> 00:00:43.910
- I played an animated version of myself

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.736
singing about Hanukkah, so.

00:00:45.736 --> 00:00:46.702
(laughing)

00:00:46.702 --> 00:00:48.190
- I played an animated version of myself

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:50.192
you know, just singing Christmas... Yeah.

00:00:50.192 --> 00:00:51.025
- Christmas and Hanukkah!

00:00:51.025 --> 00:00:51.858
- Yeah, yes, yes.

00:00:51.858 --> 00:00:53.680
And it was very hard. I went method.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:54.513
- Oh, really?

00:00:54.513 --> 00:00:55.575
- Playing myself was difficult.

00:00:55.575 --> 00:00:57.850
So, your mom, though,
is a teacher like mine.

00:00:57.850 --> 00:00:59.032
And I love my mother so much.

00:00:59.032 --> 00:00:59.865
- Yes.

00:00:59.865 --> 00:01:00.698
- And I love teachers.

00:01:00.698 --> 00:01:02.370
And you're a hardcore
lover of your momma, too.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:03.203
Right?

00:01:03.203 --> 00:01:04.036
- Yes, I love my...

00:01:04.036 --> 00:01:04.869
It'd be very weird if this was the moment

00:01:04.869 --> 00:01:06.142
that I said I hate my mom.
- [Kelly] No, no, no, no, no!

00:01:06.142 --> 00:01:06.975
(laughing)

00:01:06.975 --> 00:01:08.041
- Happy Valentine's Day!

00:01:08.041 --> 00:01:09.124
- Happy Valentine's Day, mommy!

00:01:09.124 --> 00:01:10.091
- No, I meant like...

00:01:10.091 --> 00:01:11.130
- My mom?

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:12.490
I'm happy we're doing this.

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:13.330
Mom!

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:15.244
- Mommy issues show.
- Can we turn the lights down?

00:01:15.244 --> 00:01:16.666
- I start shaking.

00:01:16.666 --> 00:01:18.515
- [Kelly] No, cause I read--
- I love her.

00:01:18.515 --> 00:01:19.685
- I read your pre-interview
and they brought up

00:01:19.685 --> 00:01:21.560
that oh, her mom is a teacher, too.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:22.843
And you were like, "I love
talking about my mom."

00:01:22.843 --> 00:01:23.676
And me too.

00:01:23.676 --> 00:01:26.251
- Yeah, she's been a Bronx
school teacher for 50 years.

00:01:26.251 --> 00:01:27.212
- [Kelly] Wow!

00:01:27.212 --> 00:01:28.531
(audience cheering)

00:01:28.531 --> 00:01:29.602
That is so cool.

00:01:29.602 --> 00:01:30.435
- [Jim] Wow.

00:01:30.435 --> 00:01:32.200
- So you guys were very kind.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.700
And you're like, my mom's
name is Joan Schwartz.

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:36.097
And one of things, they were like,

00:01:36.097 --> 00:01:37.670
"Is there a picture of you and your mom?"

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:40.200
And I noticed that all the
pictures of me as a kid

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.522
have my name on the shirt.

00:01:41.522 --> 00:01:42.510
(laughing)

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:43.391
Made me feel like,

00:01:43.391 --> 00:01:46.470
they just didn't remember
my name or something weird.

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:47.686
- You have 17 brothers and sisters.

00:01:47.686 --> 00:01:48.519
- [Kelly] Now, were you the last born?

00:01:48.519 --> 00:01:49.720
- They didn't want to get confused.

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:50.553
- Yes.

00:01:50.553 --> 00:01:52.370
They'd tell me, "Which
one are you? Ben, got it."

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:53.360
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:56.100
- So you're also a published
author. That's crazy.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.256
- I've published four books, yeah.

00:01:57.256 --> 00:01:58.592
(audience cheering)

00:01:58.592 --> 00:01:59.509
- Did you know that?

00:01:59.509 --> 00:02:00.763
- [Kelly] Do you have a life?
- I did not know that.

00:02:00.763 --> 00:02:01.721
- You published four?

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:02.554
- I know your name is Ben, though.

00:02:02.554 --> 00:02:03.387
- Wow.

00:02:03.387 --> 00:02:05.490
- Yeah, I was the publishing
house that published the books.

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:07.277
Oh, no. Yeah, I have four books.

00:02:07.277 --> 00:02:09.677
But they started off as these books that,

00:02:09.677 --> 00:02:11.763
it would be the cutest, it was called

00:02:11.763 --> 00:02:14.510
"Grandma's Dead: Breaking
Bad News and Baby Animals"

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:16.920
- [Kelly] Oh, we have
"Grandma's Dead" here actually.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.390
Yup, "Grandma's Dead".

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:20.190
- [Ben] And it's like the
cutest picture of an animal

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:22.405
and it's supposed to break ...
- Or, it's syphilis.

00:02:22.405 --> 00:02:23.395
- It's syphilis is on the back.

00:02:23.395 --> 00:02:24.380
(laughing)

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:26.930
It breaks bad news with a cute animal.

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:28.120
So you can say anything terrible and--

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.225
- Your baby's ugly?

00:02:29.225 --> 00:02:30.580
(laughing)

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:31.790
- [Jim] Aw, nice.

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:33.790
- I made that many, many
years ago, a decade ago.

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:35.650
- Oh my gosh! So wait,
they're postcards you can send

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:37.580
to someone to just cheer them up.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.025
- Yes, so that way it
like softens the blow.

00:02:40.025 --> 00:02:42.760
- [Kelly] It's not me,
it's you (laughing).

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.400
Are you in need of a card, Jim?

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.100
Do you need to tell anyone anything?

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:47.580
- Oh geez, yeah, so many, so many.

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.567
- Maybe, well, not this one but,

00:02:49.567 --> 00:02:50.438
"You're not the father?"

00:02:50.438 --> 00:02:52.390
(laughing)

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:54.210
- I haven't seen this book in a decade

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:56.169
which makes it even more
exciting that we're looking--

00:02:56.169 --> 00:02:58.466
- It'd be better if it
said, "I'm not your father."

00:02:58.466 --> 00:02:59.597
(laughing)

00:02:59.597 --> 00:03:00.430
- That'd be a tough one to grab.

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:02.532
- Yes, but it'd be funny, I'm very dark.

00:03:02.532 --> 00:03:03.580
(laughing)

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:05.720
So Ben, we've got animals coming up,

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:06.810
are you an animal person?

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:08.260
- I love animals.
- [Kelly] Me too.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:10.260
- Yeah, I very much love animals.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:11.428
I'm afraid of maybe one or two.

00:03:11.428 --> 00:03:12.708
- [Kelly] What are you afraid of,

00:03:12.708 --> 00:03:13.988
so I can bring it out?

00:03:13.988 --> 00:03:15.330
(laughing)

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:16.559
- Are you guys afraid of animals at all?

00:03:16.559 --> 00:03:17.392
- Cougars.

00:03:17.392 --> 00:03:19.684
- Cougars (laughs), yeah, mountain lions,

00:03:19.684 --> 00:03:21.095
you know what I mean, elephants.

00:03:21.095 --> 00:03:21.928
- You guys are wimps.

00:03:21.928 --> 00:03:22.761
- Grizzlies.

00:03:22.761 --> 00:03:24.629
- I don't love snakes,
but I can deal with them.

00:03:24.629 --> 00:03:25.500
- Oh, I'm not a huge fan.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.730
- And big, tarantula-y type,

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:29.500
I worked at the Bronx Zoo for a summer.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:30.554
- I worked at the Fort Worth zoo.

00:03:30.554 --> 00:03:31.387
- Really?

00:03:31.387 --> 00:03:32.220
- Yes, for a summer.

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:33.053
- Oh my goodness.

00:03:33.053 --> 00:03:33.886
- Tell me more

00:03:33.886 --> 00:03:34.744
- Okay
- I worked by the monkeys--

00:03:34.744 --> 00:03:35.881
- [Jim] Here comes the
zoo talk (laughing).

00:03:35.881 --> 00:03:37.063
- And it smelled so bad.

00:03:37.063 --> 00:03:40.220
- Yes, I worked at the petting
zoo for a little bit, too,

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.410
cause it made me feel like I had--

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:42.939
- It seems cute and then
all you smell is crap.

00:03:42.939 --> 00:03:43.772
(laughing)

00:03:43.772 --> 00:03:44.605
- Yeah, all you do is shovel crap all day.

00:03:44.605 --> 00:03:45.660
But it was very--

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:46.493
- I got kicked out of a pet store.

00:03:46.493 --> 00:03:47.326
- [Kelly] No, you have to
have a degree to shovel crap.

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:48.588
- Okay, I love this story, what happened?

00:03:48.588 --> 00:03:50.129
- For licking an iguana.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:50.983
(laughing)

00:03:50.983 --> 00:03:52.340
- Why did you lick an iguana?

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:53.173
- Just for fun.

00:03:53.173 --> 00:03:54.006
- Okay.

00:03:54.006 --> 00:03:57.169
- You don't know what an
iguana tastes like. I do.

00:03:57.169 --> 00:03:58.880
(laughing)

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:01.519
- I'm good with my imagination
on that one (laughing).

00:04:01.519 --> 00:04:02.612
(audience clapping)

00:04:02.612 --> 00:04:03.702
- What does an iguana taste like?

00:04:03.702 --> 00:04:04.833
What is lick--

00:04:04.833 --> 00:04:05.666
- It's hard to compare.

00:04:05.666 --> 00:04:06.710
- [Kelly] Like chicken?

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:07.543
- Little bitter.

00:04:07.543 --> 00:04:08.376
(laughing)

00:04:08.376 --> 00:04:09.613
- It's its own thing, yeah.

